  One wrinkle worth stating now because it shapes [38;5;153msession.js[39m: a browser global script isn't requireable from Node. So
  [38;5;153msession.js[39m ends with a small dual-export guard ([38;5;153mif (typeof module !== "undefined" && module.exports) module.exports =
[39m  [38;5;153mSession;[39m) — inert in the browser, which is what lets the test load it. The functions read [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m at call time
  rather than capturing it at load, so the test injects a fake [38;5;153mglobalThis.sessionStorage[39m and controls it.

  Five tests, all against [38;5;153msession.js[39m — [38;5;153mapp.js[39m stays untested since it's DOM-wired and the value isn't there:

