  2. [38;5;153mread[39m returns [38;5;153mnull[39m when nothing is stored
  3. [38;5;153mread[39m on a corrupted value returns [38;5;153mnull[39m [3mand[0m clears the key
  4. [38;5;153mclear[39m removes the key
  5. [38;5;153msave[39m returns [38;5;153mfalse[39m without throwing when the storage backend throws — the private-mode case

  Tests 3 and 5 are the ones earning their keep; the rest are cheap regression cover.

  That's the complete design: one new file, two edits to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, one script tag, five tests. Scope is small, but it does
  add a storage boundary, change [38;5;153mlogin()[39m's return contract, and set up the repo's first test infrastructure.
